    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11267?c=bc": {
      "title": "Associate Director- The Church in the 21st Century Center",
      "description": "Associate Director- The Church in the 21st Century Center | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Director- The Church in the 21st Century Center Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11267 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description The Church in the 21st Century Center (C21) is a catalyst and resource for the renewal of the Catholic Church, engaging critical issues facing the Church and Catholic community through conversation, programming, publications, and other creative initiatives. The Center is part of Boston College’s Division of University Mission & Ministry, which advances the University’s Jesuit, Catholic mission and supports the formation of the Boston College community. The Associate Director collaborates closely with the Director in implementing the goals and overall direction of the Church in the 21st Century Center. The Associate Director serves as managing editor of the annual C21 Resources magazine, working with guest editors and the editorial board. With strong editing and writing skills and an eye for creative design, the Associate Director serves as the primary liaison with the printer/publishing house in the development and production of each issue. The Associate Director coordinates strategic marketing initiatives, including working with multiple academic and administrative units throughout the University to plan and implement a wide array of programs; interacting with Boston College students, faculty, administrators, and prominent external scholars and speakers; and managing the Center’s marketing and promotional activity. Creativity is central to this role, and the Associate Director will help conceive and develop engaging new approaches to C21’s programming, publications, communications, and outreach. The Associate Director also serves on the C21 Advisory Committee and works collaboratively with colleagues across C21 and University Mission & Ministry. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $82,100 to $102,650; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements At minimum, a bachelor’s degree and at least eight years of work experience in a directly related professional role, including staff management, are required. A communications or theology background is preferred, along with excellent writing, editing, and presentation skills; demonstrated strength in creative design and digital marketing; and a strong understanding of contemporary issues facing the Catholic Church. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
