    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11242?c=bc": {
      "title": "Temp Delivery Driver/weekdays and evenings",
      "description": "Temp Delivery Driver/weekdays and evenings | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temp Delivery Driver/weekdays and evenings Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11242 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/16/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Driver-Temp Position Basic Function and Responsibility: Responsible for the correct receiving of all products delivered and the correct storage, placement and distribution of said products. Driving  Pizza,  and other food and beverages, to and from locations on campus. Organizes and maintains all storage areas in a sanitary and orderly manner.  Also responsible for assembly and delivery of all food and beverages. Payrate:  $27.21 per hour Requirements Qualifications: High school diploma preferred, other relevant experience may substitute for education. Knowledge and experience with food service supplies and equipment is desirable. Must be able to read and write English. The ability to repetitively lift heavy loads consistently. Must have good driving record and possess a valid Massachusetts driver's license./Must 21 years of age. Must be capable of driving up to a 25-foot fixed axle truck. The ability to lift moderately heavy objects, up to 50 pounds, on an on-going basis Must be a team player, dependable and exhibit excellent customer service skills. This is a driving position. Individuals will be required to provide information verifying a valid driver's license, submit a DMV driving record, and comply with University guidelines regarding insurability. Boston College Dining Services is seeking friendly and flexible individuals to work in temporary and on-call non-benefited positions. BC Dining Temps may work up to 18 hours per week, including late evenings and weekend. Closing Statement Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
