    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11168?c=bc": {
      "title": "Resident Director",
      "description": "Resident Director | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Resident Director Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11168 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/25/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Temporary Resident Director The mission of the Office of Residential Life is to create safe, inclusive, and well maintained living communities. We engage our community members in opportunities to develop spiritually, socially, and academically in the Jesuit, Catholic tradition of the University. Under the leadership of the Associate Vice President, Director of Residential Education, and Director of Operations, the department consists of 40 professional staff members, 24 graduate positions, 192 resident assistants, and additional student employees. Basic Function and Responsibility The Temporary Resident Director position is a temporary full-time, benefits eligible, live-in position that is expected to continue through December 2026. The Temporary Resident Director (RD) lives with, ministers to, and provides support services directly to students. The RD supervises a staff of 8-20 Resident Assistants (RAs) and Graduate Assistants (i.e. GSA, PGA, or GRD), and one Office Assistant (OA). They also oversee all operational and programmatic activities of BC’s residences and adjudicate student conduct cases. Summer responsibilities may include participation in department-wide initiatives or special project teams (e.g., Summer Student Housing or Conferences, Training Teams, etc.). By personal example, a Resident Director strives to create a safe and inclusive environment for all students by living, reflecting, and expressing the values of a Jesuit and Catholic institution, as defined by the teachings of the Catholic  Church with a special commitment to cultural diversity and social justice. Successful candidates will also be administratively strong, culturally competent, possess a Master’s degree, and have prior residence life or related student affairs experience. The Temporary Resident Director receives direct supervision from an Assistant Director, and functional supervision from multiple Assistant or Associate Directors, or the Director of Residential Education. Staff Supervision The Temporary Resident Director is responsible for the following staff supervision in their assigned community: Models for students and advocates for a commitment to the Jesuit and Catholic values of Boston College, as defined by the teachings of the Catholic Church, with special attention to cultural diversity and social justice Assists in the selection and training of undergraduate and graduate staff Plans and conducts staff meetings on a weekly basis Meets with each staff member individually on a regular basis Plans and implements staff development programs Advises staff on appropriate student and floor interventions Addresses concerning trends or behavior, as well as recognizes positive efforts Student Development/Community Standards The Temporary Resident Director is responsible for the following aspects of student development in their assigned residential community: Intentional interactions and conversations Living among students and setting an appropriate standard for residential living Oversees the programming efforts and supervises graduate assistants and RAs in program generation and responsible budgeting Serves as a Conduct Hearing Officer for violations of university policy Responds as a Resident Director on Call (RDOC) for crisis situations, including during non-business and weekend hours Provides academic and personal counseling to students, making referrals when appropriate Nurtures and supports relationships with their Campus Ministry representatives (Graduate or Resident Ministers) in the service of expressing and modeling the Jesuit and Catholic values of Boston College Engages resident population on current events including topics of diversity and equity, social justice, and being a productive community member May advise Residence Hall Council (first-year area only) or other student leadership organizations Operations The Temporary Resident Director is responsible for the following aspects of operations in their assigned community: Facilitates the opening and closing of their community Conducts health and safety inspections each semester Coordinates follow-up for all maintenance and housekeeping concerns/requests through, and with, the facilities team Conducts regular walk-throughs of community Maintains regular office hours Monday through Friday and will periodically work on nights and weekends for essential responsibilities throughout the year Facilitates check-in/check-out procedures and room changes Works with the Assistant Director of Housing Assignments & Occupancy to ensure proper occupancy records and reports On-Call Responsibilities The Temporary Resident Director is responsible for the following aspects of crisis response while on duty: Participates in the university Crisis Response duty rotation. When on duty the RD is expected to respond to crises, both on campus and in the surrounding neighborhood, in accordance with our policies and response guidelines Responds to students and parents on Residential Life issues or concerns Assists with duty during sporting and special events which may be on weekends or in the evening hours Acts as a liaison with Boston College Police Department, University Counseling Services, the Primary Care Center, faculty, and other University offices during emergencies Department and University Relations The Temporary Resident Director participates in the following department and university relations: Serves on departmental committees, and may have an opportunity to serve on division or university-wide committees Attends department and area staff meetings, in-service training programs, and one-on-one meetings with their respective supervisor Acts as a liaison with faculty, the Jesuit community, and university offices Summer responsibilities may include Training, Operations, Summer Housing, or Special Projects, as assigned by the Director or Associate Directors Assists with the implementation of university and departmental goals and objectives, and other duties as assigned In order to create a more inclusive community within the Division of Student Affairs, each staff member is expected to support division and university-wide initiatives, staff events, and serve on committees as needed. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $51,350 to $64,200; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Personnel, Counseling, or related field is strongly preferred; Bachelor’s degree required 1-3 years of progressively responsible experience working in a student affairs setting at the professional or graduate level Prior residence hall experience at the graduate or professional level preferred Comprehension and appreciation of the Jesuit and Catholic values and mission and the traditions and heritage of Boston College, and a willingness to express and abide by those values and mission Demonstrated knowledge and commitment to issues of equity, diversity, and inclusion Demonstrated understanding of student development theory Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11118?c=bc": {
      "title": "Physical Security Technician",
      "description": "Physical Security Technician | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Physical Security Technician Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11118 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/6/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Physical Security Technician (evening schedule) The Physical Security Technician reports to\nthe Manager, Integrated Security and Information Systems and directly supports\nthe technology needs of Boston College's Department of Public Safety; and\nprovides on-site support for all physical aspects of the Public Safety\nTechnology and Building Security Systems across the University including IP\nVideo Security Systems, Access Control Systems, and Panic Alarm and Intrusion\nAlarm Systems. In addition to supporting Building Security Systems, the Physical Security\nTechnician assists in supporting all physical aspects of the Public Safety\nTechnology used by the Department of Public Safety. Public Safety Technology\nincludes MDT In-Vehicle Computers, LTE Trunk Routers, 800mhz / 400mhz portable\nand base radios (excludes repeaters and their associated antennas), FirstNet\nATT and EPTT, Siren System including auditable mass notification, Smart Campus\ntechnologies including License Plate Recognition, Blue Light Emergency Phones,\nDynamic Alarm Mapping, AVL Mapping, and technologies within the Public Safety\nPrimary Communications Center and Backup Communications Center. Hiring Range: $39.47/hr to $49.35/hr. Pay rate commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Required Qualifications: Strong\ntechnical abilities to troubleshoot, support, and maintain critical physical\nsecurity equipment supporting a 24x7 operation. Five years of experience as an in-field technician with hands-on experience in the troubleshooting, repair, and installation of Public Safety Technology and Building Security Systems. Education:  Bachelor's degree preferred. Higher education experience preferred. Strong problem-solving skills, organizational skills, and project planning\nskills. Strong troubleshooting skills for problem resolution. Ability to work through problems and find solutions. Ability to manage multiple tasks with shifting priorities. Excellent customer service skills; strong commitment to customer service. Excellent coordination, collaboration, writing, and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively in a group and as a member of a project team. Knowledge of TCP/IP networking. Understanding and comfortable working with basic IP networks. Experience with Google Suite. Experience with Microsoft Excel, Word and other Microsoft Office applications. Ability to lift and carry 50 lbs. Ability to climb a ladder at least 15ft. Ability to travel across campus. Ability and experience using hand and power tools. Clean driving record required. Possess a willingness and ability to support a diverse and inclusive\nenvironment. Certifications preferred but not required: Software House - CCURE 9000 Installer Certified. Genetec Security Center Certified. Proficiency in reading and understanding security floorplans, architectural,\nand network diagrams. Lead experience preferred but not required. Preferred Technology experience. Access Control and Alarm Management Systems including Card Readers, Panic\nAlarms, Intrusion Alarms, and Intercoms. Video Security Systems (CCTV) including IP and Analog Security Cameras. Basic Computer Networking and Telecommunications. Software House - Access Control and Alarm Management Systems. Inovonics - Panic Alarms. DSC (Digital Security Controls) - Intrusion Alarm Systems. 2N and AiPhone - Intercoms. Genetec Security Center - Video Management Systems. Axis Communications - Video Security Cameras. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11091?c=bc": {
      "title": "Manager. Network Operations & UC Services",
      "description": "Manager. Network Operations & UC Services | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Manager. Network Operations & UC Services Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11091 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/31/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description The Manager, Network Operations & UC Engineering Services is a critical, high-impact \"player-coach\" leadership role responsible for steering Boston College’s enterprise communications and edge networking infrastructure through a transformative period. Serving as a key strategic partner and \"right hand\" to the Director of Network Services, the Manager will initially provide hands-on technical oversight and mentorship for the Voice Services team following a major transition to a modern Unified Communications (UC) platform. This role will lead the strategic convergence of the Voice Services and Network Operations teams into a single, unified network and communications engineering organization. The ideal candidate is a proactive operational leader with deep expertise in SIP/VoIP, strong enterprise networking fundamentals, and proven success in guiding teams through organizational change, skill uplift, and technology integration. Strategic Leadership & Organizational Evolution: - Strategic Partnership: Partner closely with the Director of Network Services to shape the long-term vision, operational roadmaps, and architectural standards for unified communications and network infrastructure. - Team Convergence & Leadership: Lead the planned integration of the Voice Services and Network Operations teams into a unified engineering unit, fostering a culture of collaboration, cross-training, and continuous improvement. - Personnel Management & Growth: Manage, mentor, and elevate individual contributors across voice and networking disciplines. Develop targeted professional growth plans to cross-skill voice engineers in modern edge networking and network engineers in VoIP/SIP architectures. - Operational Excellence: Establish standard operating procedures, incident management escalation protocols, and performance metrics across the merged organization to ensure high availability and service delivery across all campus locations. Core Technical Responsibilities Unified Communications & Applications: - Provide technical oversight for a complex enterprise communications architecture supporting 6,000+ endpoints, 120 emergency response systems, and high-volume call centers across multiple campuses. - Direct the engineering and maintenance of the Cisco Unified Communications platform, including UCS, Call Manager (CUCM), Unity, CUBE gateways, WebEx Calling/Hybrid, Cisco Endpoints, and analog gateways. - Manage inbound/outbound SIP trunking, carrier relationships, and call routing topologies. - Oversee critical communications applications and integrations, including call center platforms (T-Metrics), public safety call recording (NICE), and E911 compliance platforms (Bandwidth Technology). - Ensure seamless service integrations with enterprise identity and security systems (Microsoft AD/LDAP, Shibboleth, Duo). Enterprise Network Engineering & Infrastructure - Oversee the continuous operation, maintenance, and strategic expansion of Boston College’s edge network across 400+ Network Rooms spanning 5 campuses. - Provide high-level technical direction for enterprise switching infrastructure (800+ Extreme Networks devices) and campus-wide wireless networks (4,300+ Aruba Wireless Access Points). - Lead network topology planning, hardware lifecycle management, provisioning standards, and edge-to-core connectivity strategies. - Partner with network architecture leads to optimize network routing, VLAN configurations, quality of service for voice/video traffic, and security segmentation across wired and wireless environments. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $127,950 to $159,950; salary commensurate with relevant experience. This is an onsite position. Requirements Experience: Minimum of 8–10 years of progressive experience in network and unified communications engineering, with at least 5 years in a formal management, team lead, or senior supervisory role.  Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology Systems or related discipline. - Leadership & Change Management: Demonstrated success leading technical teams through organizational change, team mergers, or major infrastructure modernizations. - UC Expertise: Expert-level knowledge of Cisco Unified Communications Manager (CUCM), WebEx, CUBE, SIP architecture, and complex VoIP environments. - Networking Fundamentals: Strong hands-on background in enterprise edge/access networking, hardware provisioning, routing/switching, quality of service, and wireless infrastructure. - Communication: Exceptional interpersonal, strategic thinking, and leadership skills with a proven track record as an authentic mentor and collaborative leader. Preferred Qualifications - Experience in higher education or large enterprise environments managing multi-campus topologies and compliance standards (e.g., Kari’s Law / RAY BAUM’S Act for E911). - Hands-on experience or certifications with Extreme Networks hardware, ExtremeCloud IQ (XIQ), or Extreme Fabric. - Practical knowledge of Aruba Networks enterprise wireless deployments. - Experience managing contact center platforms (e.g., T-Metrics) and public safety infrastructure. - Familiarity with database/application platforms such as Oracle APEX or custom administrative integrations. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/10997?c=bc": {
      "title": "Dance Instructor",
      "description": "Dance Instructor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Dance Instructor Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req10997 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/8/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Dance Team Instructor (10 hours per week, 9 months) The Boston College Bands Program seeks a part-time Dance Team Instructor to provide instruction and support for the “Screaming Eagles” Marching Band Dance Team. Applicants should have extensive experience choreographing and instructing students in various dance forms including pom, kickline, jazz, lyrical, and hip-hop styles. Applicants must be available for our preseason Camp during the last two weeks of August from 9 AM to 10 PM in addition to weekly rehearsals during the fall and spring seasons on Tuesdays and Thursdays from 7 PM to 10 PM. In addition to seven home football games, applicants must be available for occasional special events and travel performances including potential bowl games. Each staff member in the Division of Student Affairs is expected to support division and university-wide initiatives, staff events, and serve on committees as needed. Salary: $7,918 Requirements A master’s degree in dance or dance education is preferred. Demonstrated success choreographing and teaching various dance styles Demonstrated success in managing a dance ensemble Demonstrated strong communication and interpersonal skills Must be able to relate to, teach, and motivate college students Must attend Band Camp, all rehearsals, and all performances Must manage team uniforms, costumes, props, and equipment Must be available to consult regarding programming during the off-season Must work with student leader to ensure recruiting needs are met Must meet with candidates and review auditions to select new dancers Must be available for post-season bowl travel in event of post-season football games Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/10953?c=bc": {
      "title": "Financial Systems Project Manager",
      "description": "Financial Systems Project Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Financial Systems Project Manager Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req10953 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/30/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description The Financial Systems Project Manager reports\nto the Associate Director, Financial Systems, and is responsible for supporting\nPeopleSoft Financials projects, including enhancements, integrations, system\nupgrades, and initiatives across key areas within the Financial Vice\nPresident’s division, including projects that pertain to: General Ledger,\nBudgeting, Procurement, Project Costing, third-party applications, and\nintegrations.  Primary responsibilities include leading project management\nefforts for strategic initiatives aligned with the Financial Management Systems\nfiscal year project plan, such as reviewing and enhancing current business\nprocesses with a technical solution, interface automation and providing support\nduring system upgrades and maintenance. The Financial Systems Project Manager\nserves as a technical liaison for Procure to Pay and Grant Management\nadministration to deliver ongoing process improvements, technical support, and\nmaintenance.  Additional responsibilities will include supporting\nassociated reporting, security, documentation and ad hoc projects as requested\nby the Associate Vice President, Finance and University Controller. This is an in-office position. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $110,300 to $137,900; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Bachelor’s\n     degree Proficiency\n     in PeopleSoft Financials 5-8\n     years of application implementation and development experience with\n     progressive growth in the areas of business analysis, process redesign,\n     application configuration and development and project management. Demonstrated\n     experience in leading University-wide projects and contributing at all\n     levels including project management, team leadership, mentoring functional\n     and technical staff, and reporting to senior management. Strong\n     working knowledge of financial applications, and comprehensive\n     understanding of how financial data and interfaces interact with other\n     financial applications. Experience\n     with change management software and technical tools, such as SQL,\n     PeopleTools and Application Engine. Working\n     knowledge of PeopleSoft report writer tools, nVision and Query. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/10893?c=bc": {
      "title": "Senior Research Associate (Immunology)",
      "description": "Senior Research Associate (Immunology) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Senior Research Associate (Immunology) Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req10893 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/10/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Job Title: Senior Research Associate Department: Biology, Whitney Laboratory Employment Type: On-site | Temporary | Full-Time (35hrs/week) | Exempt FTE Range: $70,000 - $100,000. Salary commensurate with relevant experience. The Whitney Laboratory is looking for an experienced immunologist to lead the flow cytometry assay development and in vivo immune monitoring activities. The successful immunologist will specifically have the below skillset and will play a critical role in data generation for translational research projects, supporting the development of novel strategies/assays/systems/analyses. Primary Responsibilities Independently design, validate, and apply immunophenotyping and functional flow cytometry panels customized to align with project goals. Independently generate, analyze, and interpret flow cytometry and other complex data sets and prepare and present presentations to the internal team. Independently operate cell sorters and analyzers, including instrument set-up, compensation control preparation, PMT voltage adjustments, experimental settings selection, sample collection (sorting), troubleshooting, and cleaning. Participate in upstream sample processing for flow cytometry analysis and sorting, including blood processing and tissue dissociation. Develop and refine immunology and flow cytometry SOPs as procedures and goals evolve and improve. Remain current with evolving cytometry advances and their application to drug discovery, proactively explore avenues to improve workflows, integrate new technology and improve data quality. Manage\n     inventory for materials, reagents, and consumables for flow cytometry and\n     immunology functions. Maintain\n     timely and detailed documentation of experimental protocols, execution,\n     data collection, analysis, and interpretation. Requirements BS 6+, MS 4+, PhD 0-2 years of research experience in\n     immunology, cell biology, or related field. 3+ years demonstrated experimental expertise in cell-based assays with a focus in flow cytometry. 3+ years of experience with one\n     or more of the following instrumentation systems: BD Aria/Fusion, BD\n     Symphony, LSR, or Fortessa. Experience\n     with human or NHP biological cell sample processing relevant to flow\n     cytometry, including working with whole blood, cell lines, and dissociated\n     tissues; prior experience working in a BL2+ environment is beneficial. Familiar\n     with techniques and instruments for mechanical and enzymatic tissue\n     dissociation. Strong oral and written communication skills with the ability to work collaboratively and to communicate complex scientific concepts with cross-disciplinary team members. Established scientific expertise, including peer-reviewed publications Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11324?c=bc": {
      "title": "Assistant Supervisor, Carpentry Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Supervisor, Carpentry Operations | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Supervisor, Carpentry Operations Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11324 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/16/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Assistant Carpentry Supervisor Location: Multi-Campus (Travel between 4–5 local campus sites required) Schedule : Monday – Friday, 7:00 AM – 3:00 PM (Essential Personnel – Subject to emergency response) Job Type: Full-time About the Role Are you a skilled trade professional who excels at leadership, scheduling, and high-level communication? We are looking for an Assistant Carpentry Supervisor to lead our day-to-day Carpentry, Paint, and Lock Shop operations across 4 to 5 campus locations. While a solid technical background in carpentry is important, this role is less about custom fabrication—which we farm out to specialty vendors—and more about keeping our campuses safe, functional, and running smoothly for our students, faculty, and administration. As a key leader for our unionized team, you will act as the bridge between hands-on trade work and campus administration. If you are tech-savvy, proactive, organized, and energized by solving daily operational challenges, we want to hear from you. Key Responsibilities; Operational Leadership & Supervision : Guide, mentor, and supervise union staff across 4–5 distinct campus locations. Inspect finished work to ensure top-quality standards. Work Order & Workflow Management: Prioritize, assign, and track daily work orders across the Carpentry, Paint, and Lock Shops using modern management tools to keep projects moving on schedule. Administrative & Stakeholder Communication: Partner effectively with school administration, department heads, and business partners. Serve as a clear, professional communicator for trade-related needs. Budget & Material Control : Order necessary tools, materials, and supplies efficiently while managing shop budgets—with a strong focus on controlling and authorizing overtime. Multi-Task Management: Balance multiple ongoing work orders, maintenance routines, and unexpected daily priorities without missing deadlines. Emergency Preparedness : Serve as essential personnel, responding swiftly to campus emergencies when needed to maintain safety and security. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $86,000 to $107,500; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Qualifications & Skills Experience: Minimum of 5 years of supervisory experience in construction, facilities maintenance, or managing a large, complex building portfolio. Education & Credentials: Associate or Bachelor’s Degree preferred, or active State Licensure / Construction Trade Certifications. Tech Proficiency: Comfortable with digital tools, including Microsoft Office, Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Chat, Drive), and Smartsheet. Experience with electronic work order systems and digital timekeeping is a major plus. Leadership & Soft Skills: Strong interpersonal, analytical, and problem-solving skills with the ability to make sound operational decisions independently. Licensure: Must hold and maintain a valid Driver’s License. Physical Requirements Ability to physically navigate multiple campus properties daily. Comfort walking significant distances, climbing stairs, and using ladders as standard parts of site inspections and emergency response. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11322?c=bc": {
      "title": "Construction Building Envelope Manager",
      "description": "Construction Building Envelope Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Construction Building Envelope Manager Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11322 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description The Capital Projects Management Department is responsible for the engineering, planning, documentation and construction management of Boston College’s Capital Improvement Plan. The plan is coordinated into two strategic components: the Annual Capital Plan and the Major Construction Plan, which comprise as many as 150 ongoing projects throughout the calendar year. The Construction Building Envelope Manager reports to the Associate Director, Annual Capital Projects and is responsible for management of capital construction projects supporting the Annual Capital Plan through all phases from planning, design and construction. Responsibilities include implementing best practices for construction project delivery including scope, schedule, estimating and budget development, risk management, procurement strategies and contract administration and project cost control. The CPM will work with consultants and Boston College stakeholders including Facilities Management, to develop design and construction documents. The CPM is responsible to maintain quality communications with BC Departments, and project stakeholders, using management software PMWeb to report project schedule, progress and budget control. The position requires extensive knowledge of good building, construction and project management practices and processes.  A broad understanding of building envelope systems, building mechanical, electrical, plumbing and fire alarm systems, building finishes and site utilities is required. Proven experience managing multiple projects with aggressive project schedules.The work requires strict adherence to University budgets and schedules due to the annual budget process and the academic calendar.  Ability to organize and manage teams, including internal design and operations staff, external contractors and design consultants. Emphasis on planning, coordination, and execution of the institution’s annual building envelope assessment and repair program. This role ensures that all roofs, façades, drainage systems, and related envelope components are proactively inspected, documented, maintained, and repaired in alignment with institutional priorities, risk management goals, and long‑term capital planning. Basic Requirements: ●      At least 5 years of progressively responsible experience in architecture, engineering or construction management. ●      Experience with project management of facilities, renovation and new construction for an institution of higher education or other large owner is preferred. ●      Bachelor’s Degree in construction, architecture, engineering or related field ●      Experience with financial and project management/control systems, such as PeopleSoft, CAD, and PMWeb. ●      Able to manage and adapt to changes in scope and to work both independently or as part of a team. ●      Maintain current knowledge of all applicable regulations and codes for design and construction projects ●      Position requires ability to access all areas of construction sites including climbing ladders to assess conditions and perform inspections of existing facilities. ●      Prepare written and graphic presentations. ●      Perform other related duties as assigned Requirements Preferred Qualifications: ●      10 or more years of construction project management experience. ●      Previous experience as an Owner’s Rep at a higher education academic or institutional organization desired. ●      Experience with or a strong understanding of the unique requirements and challenges of building roof systems, facades, drainage and envelopes. ●      Strong knowledge of various project delivery methods including CMR/GMP and Lump sum. ●      Architecture, engineering or construction background. ●      Strong understanding of mechanical, electrical, plumbing and structural and building envelope systems. ●      Experience managing multiple projects simultaneously from planning and design through construction completion with budgets up to $10 million. ●      Prepare financial analyses and preliminary total project cost estimates. Establish, track, and manage budget during the course of the project. ●      Ability to develop project budgets, forecasts and reports ●      Ability to direct consultants and contractors for design and construction quality. ●      Ability to manage decision making processes in a consensus-oriented institutional environment. ●      Current Massachusetts Construction Supervisor License or the willingness to obtain one within one year. Title and salary commensurate with relevant experience based on the following titles and full-time equivalent hiring ranges: - Construction Project Manager: $107,350 - $134,200; 5+ years related professional experience - Project Manager: $97,200 - $121,500; 3-5 years related professional experience - Assistant Project Manager: $79,900 - $99,900; 1-3 years experience Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11321?c=bc": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager - Corcoran Commons",
      "description": "Assistant Manager - Corcoran Commons | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Manager - Corcoran Commons Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11321 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/15/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Manage, organize, and participate in the daily dining service activities.  Must demonstrate hands on personnel management, customer service, pro-active leadership, and have ability to achieve quality food sanitation and customer service goals.  Perform all responsibilities at a high level of professionalism and confidentiality. Characteristic Duties: -Determine and clearly, proactively, and concisely communicate, demonstrate and explain work assignments and expectations. - Demonstrate accurate oral and written communication skills. -Maintain unit sanitation, safety and appearance, ensure food quality standards. - Participate in planning employee schedules and adjustments including authorizing and assigning overtime and to call in off-duty staff as needed. -Participate in the hiring process including interviewing of prospective applicants and participate in hiring decisions. -Train, instruct, and assess daily and annual performance of job duties to ensure high quality food presentation, sanitation, and customer service. -Proactively respond to inquiries and needs of employees and customers. -Assign and reassign employees to meet daily operational needs; ensure accurate time management for employees. -Participate in the corrective action process with authority to provide counseling, oral warning, and written warnings. -Understand and demonstrate pro-active fiscal management responsibilities, including payroll, scheduling, inventory, waste, ordering, time and cash reconciliation. -Responsible for operation and maintenance of food service and point of sales equipment.  Communicate equipment problems via established protocol. - Demonstrate, teach, supervise and monitor cashier functions, operation, and reports before, during, and after meal periods. -Perform necessary record keeping as directed such as sales reports, register reports, product movement, attendance and performance records, equipment maintenance, and payroll. -Manage, supervise, coordinate, and participate in catered events which may be in operating unit or other locations on campus as directed. -Perform other related duties as assigned. Position Details: Department: 023109 - BCDS Corcoran Commons Position: 00004283 - Assistant Manager Grade: 2ND Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $67,350 to $84,200; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Education: Bachelor's degree preferred, Associate's Degree required or equivalent combination of experience. Computer literacy is desirable. Serv Safe Food Safety Certification. Experience: Three- to five-years food and beverage experience in progressively responsible positions. Supervisory experience with ability to motivate. High quality standards as well as exceptional knowledge of food service procedures and practices. Skills: Ability to manage and work effectively with students, faculty, and staff clientele in high volume and fast-paced environment. Must have outstanding communication, human relations, and interpersonal skills and be able to coordinate and gain the cooperation of a large and diverse staff. Bilingual English/Spanish skills helpful. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including some evenings and weekends throughout the year. Self-motivated, highly energetic, organized, and results-oriented professional. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
