    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11354?c=bc": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Tax Reform & the Common Good",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Tax Reform & the Common Good | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Director, Tax Reform & the Common Good Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11354 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Reporting to Professor Ray D. Madoff, Faculty Director, the Assistant Director oversees the financial, operational, and administrative functions of the Initiative for Tax Reform and the Common Good at Boston College Law School. The Faculty Director directs the Initiative's substance and priorities; the Assistant Director administers the Initiative’s budget and gift funds, keeps the Director’s schedule, correspondence, and the Initiative’s logistics running smoothly, coordinates outside consultants and experts, tracks deliverables and timelines, and manages the Initiative’s social media and marketing presence. This position may be structured as either part-time or full-time — both will be considered. The appointment runs through May 31, 2028, with a strong likelihood of extension based on continued funding. Some early morning, evening, or weekend work may be required. Please include a cover letter describing your interest in the role and the mission with your application. Full-Time Equivalent Hiring Range: $61,050 to $76,300; salary commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements ●      Bachelor’s degree required; JD degree preferred. ●      2 years of related experience in program administration, project management, finance, or executive support; higher education, law, or policy/advocacy setting preferred. ●      A genuine commitment to the Initiative’s mission is essential to this role. We are seeking someone who cares deeply about building a fairer, more coherent tax system — not simply an administrator, but a colleague who is personally invested in the cause and motivated by the prospect of turning sound tax-policy ideas into real legislative change. ●      Experience managing budgets, financial tracking, and reconciliations; PeopleSoft Financials experience preferred. ●      Advanced-level experience with standard office software (Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, Adobe, online calendars, databases, mail merges). ●      Strong organizational and project-management skills; extremely detail-oriented; able to manage multiple projects and complex calendaring. ●      Experience managing social media and supporting marketing or communications. ●      Excellent written and oral communication; skilled at composing correspondence and recording minutes. ●      Self-starter who works well independently and in a small team, with sound judgment in a fast-paced environment. ●      Discretion and the ability to handle confidential matters; a high degree of professionalism, tact, and patience. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11353?c=bc": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Gabelli Presidential Scholars (Temporary)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Gabelli Presidential Scholars (Temporary) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Administrative Assistant, Gabelli Presidential Scholars (Temporary) Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11353 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Job Title: Administrative Assistant (Temporary) Department: Gabelli Presidential Scholars Salary: $25/hr. Salary commensurate with relevant experience. Assists with the administrative and logistical aspects, as well as the delivery of activities, of the Gabelli Presidential Scholars Program (GPSP). Handles all budget transactions for department, helps with the production of various GPSP publications, maintains website, registers each of the 3 overseas trips on the University’s Travel Registry and performs additional administrative and support services for the Director and Associate Director as assigned. This position requires some weeknight work and some weekend work, especially for the GPSP Selection Process and the Senior Reception. Major Duties and Responsibilities Assists with the administrative and logistical aspects as well as the delivery of activities of the Program. Handles budget transactions such as paying invoices, requesting student stipends, wire transfers and financial transactions for Stamps Scholarship students. Handles website updates. Handles production of the annual GPSP Directory of Scholars and Alumni with the Associate Director’s guidance. Responsible for the Travel registry for 3 group trips per year. Responsible for ordering supplies and keeping the supply closet stocked as needed. Assists with operations of 4-day GPSP Selection Process. Helps maintain the databases for current GPSP Alumni and “Friends” of the GPSP and keeps Scholars’ records up-to-date. Performs additional administrative and support services for the Director and Associate Director as assigned. Requirements Education : Bachelor’s Degree and previous office/administrative experience required. Skills/Knowledge: Position requires a keen sense of empathy, exceptional judgment, the ability to handle pressure and to be able to juggle multiple projects simultaneously. Also, the position requires discretion and the ability to handle confidential and sensitive material. Person must be able to exhibit grace under pressure, and successfully meet deadlines. Excellent interpersonal, communication and organizational skills. Ideal candidate would have experience in: Peoplesoft, Microsoft Office, InDesign, Photoshop, Slate, and Apex. Ability to master other technology as needed. Closing Statement Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11352?c=bc": {
      "title": "Fire Safety Officer",
      "description": "Fire Safety Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Fire Safety Officer Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11352 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Reporting to the Fire Safety Manager, the Fire Safety Officer will support and coordinate activities related to fire and life safety programs, ensure compliance with fire safety protocols and evaluate existing and new fire protection systems and make recommendations to the Fire Safety Manager for adequacy and regulatory compliance. Specific functions include: · Serving as the institutional liaison with local fire safety authorities and assisting the Fire Safety Manager in the administration and management of both the comprehensive fire and life safety programs for the University. · Coordinating inspections, managing licenses, permits, etc. to ensure compliance with fire safety protocols and making recommendations of any necessary corrective actions and ensuring implementation of those corrective actions. · Assisting in the development of fire and life safety plans, providing OSHA emergency evacuation training, organizing and leading drills and exercises. · Assisting University personnel with understanding of requirements for the effective use of related plans, procedures, guidelines, Federal, State and local requirements and consensus codes; · Inspecting facilities to identify any potential hazards needing correction, including occupancy loads, building egress paths and patterns, life safety equipment access and impairments, emergency signage, and unique hazards present in research laboratories, administrative, academic and residence-style buildings. · Working closely with Facilities Services to ensure that all construction and fire prevention related permits are filed in a timely manner with the local fire safety authorities including but not limited to hot work permits, smoke detector bagging permits, NFPA 241 affidavits, special event and assembly area permits, temporary dumpster placements, food trucks, portable generators, fuel storage, and tents. · Sharing on-call responsibilities with other members of EHS team and being available to respond to emergency alerts 24/7 (one week per month) Requirements Bachelor’s degree in fire safety, engineering, protection and/or related science discipline. 5 years of experience and professional course work in fire and life safety, emergency management or related fields, preferably command experience. Strong working knowledge of federal, state and local fire safety regulations and codes. Must be skilled in assessing and implementing fire safety compliance programs and working with a diverse group of faculty, staff, students and regulators. Must have a valid Massachusetts driver’s license Must be capable of lifting fire safety equipment up to 30 pounds Must be capable of climbing ladders and inspecting equipment rooms 20 hours/52 weeks. Hiring range: $39.89 - $49.86 hourly; salary commensurate with experience. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
    },
    "https://bc.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/2/home/requisition/11350?c=bc": {
      "title": "Lead Food Service Worker - Corcoran Commons",
      "description": "Lead Food Service Worker - Corcoran Commons | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lead Food Service Worker - Corcoran Commons Chestnut Hill, MA, United States | req11350 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Boston College Introduction Founded in 1863, Boston College is a Jesuit, Catholic university located six miles from downtown Boston with an enrollment of 9,654 full-time undergraduates and 5,072 graduate and professional students. Ranked 37 among national universities, Boston College has 923 full-time and 1,336 FTE faculty, 2,822 non-faculty employees, an operating budget of $1.4 billion, and an endowment in excess of $3.9 billion. Job Description Lead Food Service Worker Basic Function and Responsibility Supervises and participates in the routine tasks to prepare, serve and store vegetables, salads, sliced meats, baked goods and desserts. Cashier duties when necessary. Sets up, serves, and cleans up. Directs other food service workers or student employees assigned to work station. Moderate to heavy lifting is necessary. Characteristic Duties -Under general supervision, performs routine supportive tasks such as cutting, mixing, slicing, assembling, serving and storing food. -Assumes lead responsibility in work areas as assigned. -Transports food and supplies to service areas and assembles and replenishes food as directed. -Participates in the cleaning, sanitation, and safety of assigned work areas and equipment as directed. -As directed, assists in training of food service workers and students assigned to work area. -May assist in the bussing of trays in dining room. -Assists in the setup of work area as directed. -Assists in the execution of catered events as directed. -May perform cashier duties as assigned. -May be assigned other duties during slow periods such as semester breaks, holidays and the summer. -Performs all other reasonable duties as assigned. Supervision Received Reports to the Kitchen Manager in assigned unit, while receiving functional direction from unit chef and/or first cook. Supervision Exercised Assist in the monitoring of work by food service workers and other support personnel. Position Details: Department: BCDS Corcoran Commons Position: Lead Food Service Worker- 35 Hours Grade: D Hiring Range: $27.21/hr to $30.23/hr. Pay rate commensurate with relevant experience. Requirements Qualifications Education:   High School Diploma preferred. Additional relevant experience may substitute for education. NRA ServSafe certification and MRA Allergen certification preferred. Experience: Minimum of 2 years? experience in a large volume food operation. Supervisory experience preferred. Skills: Must be able to read and write English. Must be able to work effectively in a fast-paced operation with a diverse staff. Must have good human relations skills. Must be able to operate basic kitchen equipment. Must be able to lift moderately heavy objects, up to 50 pounds, on an ongoing basis. Closing Statement Boston College offers a broad and competitive range of benefits depending on your job classification eligibility: Tuition remission for Employees Tuition remission for Spouses and Children who meet eligibility requirements Generous Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Low-Cost Life Insurance Eligibility for both University-Funded 401k and Employer-Sponsored 403b Retirement Plans Paid Holidays Annually Generous Sick and Vacation Pay Additional benefits can be found on https://www.bc.edu/employeehandbook Boston College conducts pre-employment background checks as part of the hiring process. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category, including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination . Apply Now Share Save Job As an applicant for employment, you are entitled to a copy of Boston College’s Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report, located on the Campus Security Information Page . This web page contains Boston College’s campus safety program, which includes the University’s safety policies and campus crime statistics reported during the previous three years, as well as the University’s fire safety program. To request a paper copy of this report, please contact the Boston College Police Department at 617-552-4446. Boston College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected category including disability and protected veteran status. Boston College's Notice of Nondiscrimination can be viewed at https://www.bc.edu/nondiscrimination ."
